## Overview

**Kyrelix Security Advisor** is an Android application that brings account security guidance and authenticator utilities together. The goal is to help people understand their accounts' security posture, use stronger credentials, and find the appropriate official steps to improve protection.

> **Important:** This is a public **information and release repository**, not the application source-code repository. This repository does not provide buildable Android or Flutter source code.

## Main capabilities

- **Authenticator tools:** TOTP/HOTP accounts and QR-based enrollment, including camera and gallery import.
- **Account Security Advisor:** a central view of linked accounts and security findings.
- **Official provider connections:** approved integrations may retrieve the security data that each provider API actually exposes; GitHub integration is under development/testing.
- **Clear results:** verified positive, actionable warning, confirmed issue, permission/API unavailable, or not assessed. A missing permission is not proof of an insecure account.
- **Password Advisor:** locally generated password suggestions with optional memorable hints. Password strength is not inferred from third-party account access.
- **Passkey and device guidance:** links to official security settings where direct verification is not supported.
- **Kyrelix sessions:** information about the application's own Appwrite sessions, when signed in; session counts are not necessarily distinct device counts.

## How account checks work

When a supported provider is connected and the user authorizes the requested permissions, Kyrelix attempts to retrieve **only the facts exposed by that provider's authorized API**. Results are shown automatically where implemented; they are not fabricated when access is unavailable. No universal third-party API can expose all connected devices, passkeys, passwords or authentication settings across all services.

## Availability

Development and testing are ongoing. No public download URL or store listing is claimed here until an official release is published. Check the [Releases](../../releases) section of this repository for announcements and verify release provenance before installing any APK.

## Privacy and security

See [Privacy overview](docs/PRIVACY.md) for the planned/known data categories and items requiring verification prior to launch. Please use the guidance in [SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md) to report security concerns **privately**. Never post TOTP seeds, recovery codes, access tokens, device session data, passwords or personal account details in public issues.

